{"term":"kapalı","lang":"tr","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"honor_shame_economy","subcategory":"inhibition","concept":"sexual_inhibition","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"euphemism","crude":10,"technical":10,"recognition_pct_current":88,"recognition_pct_peak":88,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Lit. 'closed/shut'; used euphemistically for sexual inhibition or reserve; also independently means 'veiled/hijab-wearing,' layering Islamic-modesty connotation onto the sexual sense.","english_term":"closed off","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Dual meaning: (1) sexually inhibited/reserved; (2) wearing the hijab ('kapalı kadın' = veiled woman); both senses converge on Turkish Islamic modesty norms."}
{"term":"buz gibi","lang":"tr","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"desire_arousal_descriptors","subcategory":"frigidity","concept":"sexual_frigidity","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"euphemism","crude":18,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":90,"recognition_pct_peak":90,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Lit. 'like ice'; idiom for complete sexual frigidity, implying utter absence of sexual warmth or responsiveness.","english_term":"cold as ice","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Intensified form of 'soğuk' (cold); the ice simile amplifies frigidity to an extreme; used for emotional coldness generally, not exclusively in sexual contexts."}
{"term":"isteksiz","lang":"tr","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"desire_arousal_descriptors","subcategory":"low_desire","concept":"low_libido","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":8,"technical":25,"recognition_pct_current":90,"recognition_pct_peak":90,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Lacking desire or willingness; describes absent or low sexual drive, or simple reluctance to engage in sexual activity.","english_term":"unwilling","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"'istek' = desire/wish; '-siz' = without (privative suffix); broadly neutral in register; used freely outside sexual contexts for general unwillingness."}
{"term":"soğuk kadın","lang":"tr","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"desire_arousal_descriptors","subcategory":"frigidity","concept":"sexual_frigidity","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":25,"technical":10,"recognition_pct_current":83,"recognition_pct_peak":83,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Lit. 'cold woman'; colloquial phrase for a sexually unresponsive or frigid woman, used pejoratively.","english_term":"cold woman","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Compound of 'soğuk' (cold) + 'kadın' (woman); applied exclusively to women; implicitly places blame for sexual unavailability on the woman."}
{"term":"taşlık","lang":"tr","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"desire_arousal_descriptors","subcategory":"frigidity","concept":"sexual_frigidity","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":55,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":55,"recognition_pct_peak":55,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Lit. 'gizzard' or 'rocky/stony place'; crude slang for extreme sexual frigidity, implying a woman is as hard and unyielding as stone.","english_term":"stone-cold","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Primary meanings are bird gizzard and rocky terrain; the sexual application metaphorizes stony hardness as total sexual coldness; more regional and colloquial with uneven national recognition."}
{"term":"bekâret","lang":"tr","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"honor_shame_economy","subcategory":"virginity","concept":"defloration","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"moral_religious","crude":10,"technical":40,"recognition_pct_current":95,"recognition_pct_peak":95,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Virginity; the state of never having had sexual intercourse, carrying profound honor-based moral and legal significance in Turkish culture.","english_term":"virginity","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Arabic loanword (bikārat); 'bekâret testi' (virginity testing) remains a contested legal and social practice in Turkey; the concept carries far heavier honor-shame weight than English 'virginity.' Registry maps to defloration as the closest available slug."}
{"term":"kızlık","lang":"tr","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"honor_shame_economy","subcategory":"virginity","concept":"defloration","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":15,"technical":25,"recognition_pct_current":93,"recognition_pct_peak":93,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Lit. 'girlhood' or 'maidenhood'; used as a synonym for virginity; in compound 'kızlık zarı' specifically denotes the hymen.","english_term":"maidenhood","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"'kız' = girl/virgin; '-lık' = abstract noun suffix; 'kızlık zarı' (lit. 'maidenhood membrane') is the standard Turkish term for hymen; overlaps with but is softer in register than 'bekâret.'"}
